---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Terms of Service – Wawe Journal" description="The terms that govern your use of Wawe Journal, including subscriptions, cancellation and refunds.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="pill anim" style="--d:.05s"><b>Terms</b></span>
      <h1 class="anim" style="--d:.15s">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="page-meta anim" style="--d:.3s">Last updated: October 31, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose reveal">
        <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
        <p>These terms govern your use of Wawe Journal (wawejournal.com), a trading journal and performance analytics service based in İstanbul, Türkiye ("Wawe Journal", "we", "us", "our"). By creating an account or using the service, you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the service.</p>

        <h2>2. The service</h2>
        <p>Wawe Journal lets you log, import and sync your trades, analyze your performance, track prop firm rules and practice strategies with backtest replay. Specifically:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Broker connections are <strong>read-only</strong>. We import your trading history; we never place, change or close orders, and we never move funds on your accounts.</li>
          <li>Backtest replay is a <strong>simulation</strong>. Orders placed in backtest accounts are not sent to any broker or market.</li>
          <li>Prop firm trackers are planning tools. They are not official evaluations by any prop firm.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. No financial advice</h2>
        <p class="callout">Wawe Journal is not a broker, investment adviser or financial institution and does not give investment, financial or trading advice. All statistics, reports, simulations and other outputs are for information and education only. Trading involves substantial risk, and past or backtested performance does not guarantee future results. You alone are responsible for your trading decisions and their outcomes.</p>

        <h2>4. Accounts</h2>
        <p>You must be at least 18 years old to use the service. You must give accurate information and keep your login details safe. You are responsible for all activity under your account, and you must tell us immediately at <a href="mailto:support@wawejournal.com">support@wawejournal.com</a> if you suspect unauthorized access.</p>

        <h2>5. Plans and pricing</h2>
        <p>Wawe Journal offers a free Starter plan and a paid Pro plan, billed monthly or yearly. Current prices are shown on our <a href="/#pricing">pricing section</a> before you buy. Prices are in US dollars. Applicable sales tax or VAT may be added at checkout depending on your location.</p>

        <h2>6. Payments</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Card and other fiat payments</strong> are processed by Creem, our Merchant of Record and authorized reseller. Creem is the seller of record for these purchases, handles the payment, sales tax and receipts, and your purchase is also subject to Creem's terms.</li>
          <li><strong>Cryptocurrency payments</strong> are processed by NOWPayments. A crypto payment is a one-time prepayment for one billing period (monthly or yearly) and does not renew automatically.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Subscriptions, renewal and cancellation</h2>
        <p>Pro subscriptions paid through Creem renew automatically at the end of each billing period until you cancel. You can cancel at any time from your account settings or through the Creem customer portal link in your receipt email. After you cancel, you keep Pro access until the end of the period you have already paid for, and you will not be charged again. Crypto prepayments simply expire at the end of the paid period.</p>

        <h2>8. Refunds</h2>
        <p>If you are not happy with Pro, you can request a full refund within 14 days of your first payment for a plan by emailing <a href="mailto:support@wawejournal.com">support@wawejournal.com</a>. Renewal payments are not refundable unless required by law, but you can cancel at any time to stop future charges. Refunds for card payments are issued by Creem to the original payment method. Refunds for crypto payments are sent in the original cryptocurrency, less network fees. Nothing in these terms limits any refund rights you have under mandatory consumer protection law.</p>

        <h2>9. Partner program</h2>
        <p>Approved partners receive a referral code that gives their audience a discount and earns the partner a commission on qualifying subscriptions. Commissions are paid by us in cryptocurrency (BTC or LTC) to the wallet address the partner provides, after a minimum balance of $20 and our review of the payout request. Commissions on refunded or fraudulent purchases, self-referrals and misleading promotion are void. We may change or end the program, or remove a partner who breaks these terms.</p>

        <h2>10. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>access or try to access other users' data or accounts;</li>
          <li>scrape, copy or resell the service or its data with bots or scripts;</li>
          <li>overload, attack or interfere with our systems;</li>
          <li>use the service for anything unlawful or fraudulent;</li>
          <li>reverse engineer the service, except where the law allows it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>11. Your content</h2>
        <p>You own the trades, notes, screenshots and other content you add. You give us permission to store and process that content only to provide the service to you. You can export or delete your content at any time.</p>

        <h2>12. Third-party services and trademarks</h2>
        <p>Some features depend on third-party services such as broker APIs, which can change, fail or return delayed or incomplete data. Please check important figures against your broker's official statements. MetaTrader, cTrader, TradingView, FTMO and other broker, platform and prop firm names are trademarks of their respective owners. Wawe Journal is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.</p>

        <h2>13. Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>We work to keep Wawe Journal available and accurate, but we cannot guarantee that it will be uninterrupted or error-free. We may add, change or remove features. If we make a change that materially reduces a paid plan, we will tell you in advance.</p>

        <h2>14. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, the service is provided "as is", and we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, trading losses, or losses caused by data errors, sync failures or third-party outages. Our total liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.</p>

        <h2>15. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>You can stop using the service and ask us to delete your account at any time. We may suspend or close accounts that break these terms or put the service or other users at risk. Where possible we will tell you why.</p>

        <h2>16. Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Türkiye. Disputes will be handled by the courts and enforcement offices of İstanbul. If you are a consumer, you also keep the protection of the mandatory laws of the country where you live and may bring a claim there.</p>

        <h2>17. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. We will change the date at the top of this page and notify you of significant changes by email or in the app. If you keep using the service after a change takes effect, you accept the updated terms.</p>

        <h2>18. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these terms or your subscription? Email <a href="mailto:support@wawejournal.com">support@wawejournal.com</a>. We answer within 2 business days.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="page-actions">
        <a href="/" class="btn btn-line" data-i18n="common.back_home">← Back to Home</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
